at first glance visitors may not realize  that inside this mosque is a  multicolored secret  [Music]  located in iran the nazir al-mukh mosque  is commonly known as the pink mosque due  to the rose-colored tiles that cover the  interior however this is far from the  only color found inside  a wall of stained glass windows turns  the interior into a rainbow wonderland  [Music]  built in 1888 the mosque took 12 years  to complete  nasir almaq features plenty of  traditional islamic architecture  elements such as the arches and the  central structure however the presence  of stained glass windows a design  element relatively rare for mosques  makes this particular mosque a unique  and stunning sight to see  the stained glass in nasiromoc was built  to catch the morning sunlight as it  reflects off the walls and the brightly  colored persian rugs on the floor  [Music]  the hope and intention was for the  colors to create a peaceful atmosphere  during early morning prayer  [Music]  the nasir almaq mosque has become as  much of a destination for visitors  seeking the perfect photo as those who  still worship under the rainbow of light  [Music]
 

